# Dynamic respawn (server/data/scripts/chaos/respawn.lua, server/README.md "Spawn density and respawn"): the stock engine
# reads each spawn's interval from the spawn file once and has no way to change it at runtime. This adds
#   Game.setSpawnIntervalPercent(percent[, fromPosition, toPosition])
#       every map spawn, or every spawn whose centre lies in the box, respawns after percent of its spawntime
#       (clamped to 10-1000, the result never under the engine's 10 s minimum); returns how many spawns were set
# The percent is kept per spawn (100 = stock, also after a map reload) and used in Spawn::checkSpawn and when the
# next check is scheduled. When it drops while a check is pending, the spawn checks again after 1 s, so a lower
# percent takes effect at once. The rule "no respawn while a player sees the spot" and rateSpawn are unchanged.
# respawn.lua sets a lower percent where several players hunt close together and puts it back to 100 when they leave;
# without this patch it does nothing (it logs once that the engine function is missing).
# Only spawn.cpp / spawn.h / luascript.cpp / luascript.h change.
# Apply in the server source root after 0001-0021: patch -p1 < 0022-dynamic-respawn.patch, then rebuild.
